    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2/SiO2 repeated 12 times (24 total finite layers). Initialize all layer thicknesses uniformly random within 30-150 nm range. Use simulated annealing optimizer with initial temperature 0.1, cooling rate 0.95, minimum temperature 0.001. Optimize thicknesses to maximize mean transmittance in 800-1500 nm band and mean reflectance in 200-400 nm band at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Apply ±15 nm absolute normal thickness tolerance for robustness evaluation. Total layer count fixed at 24. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 200-400 nm, 800-1500 nm. soft objectives: High transmission in 800-1500 nm band; High reflection in 200-400 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low transmission in 200-400 nm band; Low reflection in 800-1500 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layers <= 30; Materials limited to HfO2 and SiO2.",
